0:{"buildId":"vRbee8nUQznTUIaT_jJ-I","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","main",null,{"className":"relative mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-5 pt-24 md:gap-6","children":["$","section",null,{"id":"docs-content","className":"relative w-full overflow-hidden mx-auto max-w-6xl rounded-4xl bg-page-offset/90 shadow-panel px-6 py-8 sm:px-10 sm:py-10","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_20rem] lg:items-start","children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"min-w-0 wrap-break-word text-content-active","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-center","children":["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full bg-secondary text-content-inverse px-4 py-1","children":"Documentation"}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"markdown-content","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"id":"k8s-incident-triage-assistant","children":"K8S Incident Triage Assistant"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"{: .no_toc }"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":["<span class=\"label label-blue\">","{{ page.subcategory }}","</span>"]}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":["The ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Incident Triage Assistant"}]," plugin provides an automated diagnostic agent that investigates Kubernetes workload failures on-demand, triggered by Alertmanager webhooks or manual developer actions. When a pod is ",["$","pre","code-0",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"OOMKilled"}]}],", an image fails to pull, or a container enters a crash loop, the assistant collects bounded cluster diagnostics, classifies the failure signature, and generates a cited, evidence-backed triage report detailing likely root causes and next steps."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":["To ensure strict production safety, the assistant is ",["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"purely read-only and diagnostic"}],". It leverages a secure cluster driver contract to aggregate logs, events, and container states, but it lacks any mutation capabilities - meaning it can never execute restarts, rollbacks, or scaling actions."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"id":"key-features","children":"Key Features"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Deterministic Failure Classification"}],": Maps errors (",["$","pre","code-0",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"OOMKilled"}]}],", ",["$","pre","code-1",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"ImagePullBackOff"}]}],", ",["$","pre","code-2",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"CrashLoopBackOff"}]}],", ",["$","pre","code-3",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"ProgressDeadlineExceeded"}]}],") directly to tailored evidence-collection plans without relying on model-driven discovery."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Bounded Log Collection"}],": Safeguards system memory by strictly capping log collection for terminated or restarting containers using ",["$","pre","code-0",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"maxLogBytes"}]}]," and ",["$","pre","code-1",{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"maxLogContainers"}]}]," limits."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Citation-Backed Diagnostics"}],": Generates a report separating observed cluster data from model inference, explicitly tracking claims back to specific evidence IDs."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Fail-Safe Fallbacks"}],": Reverts automatically to a pre-defined, deterministic list of failure-class causes if the model fails validation or leaves claims uncited."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Automated Data Redaction"}],": Secures sensitive workloads by stripping bearer tokens, AWS keys, PEM private keys, and credentials from all evidence items prior to prompting."]}],"\n",["$","li","li-5",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Multi-Turn Incident Memory"}],": Maintains a persistent conversation session allowing operators to ask iterative, follow-up troubleshooting questions about the active failure."]}],"\n","$L2","\n"]}],"\n","$L3","\n","$L4","\n","$L5","\n","$L6","\n","$L7","\n","$L8","\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e","\n","$L2f","\n","$L30","\n","$L31","\n","$L32","\n","$L33","\n","$L34","\n","$L35","\n","$L36","\n","$L37","\n","$L38","\n","$L39","\n","$L3a","\n","$L3b","\n","$L3c","\n","$L3d","\n","$L3e","\n","$L3f","\n","$L40","\n","$L41","\n","$L42","\n","$L43","\n","$L44","\n","$L45","\n","$L46","\n","$L47","\n","$L48","\n","$L49","\n","$L4a","\n","$L4b","\n","$L4c","\n","$L4d","\n","$L4e","\n","$L4f","\n","$L50","\n","$L51","\n","$L52","\n","$L53","\n","$L54","\n","$L55","\n","$L56","\n","$L57","\n","$L58","\n","$L59","\n","$L5a","\n","$L5b","\n","$L5c","\n","$L5d","\n","$L5e","\n","$L5f","\n","$L60","\n","$L61","\n","$L62","\n","$L63","\n","$L64","\n","$L65","\n","$L66","\n","$L67","\n","$L68","\n","$L69","\n","$L6a","\n","$L6b","\n","$L6c","\n","$L6d","\n","$L6e","\n","$L6f","\n","$L70","\n","$L71","\n","$L72","\n","$L73","\n","$L74","\n","$L75","\n","$L76","\n","$L77","\n","$L78","\n","$L79","\n","$L7a","\n","$L7b","\n","$L7c","\n","$L7d","\n","$L7e","\n","$L7f","\n","$L80","\n","$L81","\n","$L82","\n","$L83","\n","$L84","\n","$L85","\n","$L86","\n","$L87","\n","$L88","\n","$L89","\n","$L8a","\n","$L8b","\n","$L8c","\n","$L8d","\n","$L8e","\n","$L8f","\n","$L90"]}]]}],"$L91"]}]}]}],null,"$L92"]}],"isPartial":"$@93","staleTime":"$94","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L95","isPartial":"$@96","staleTime":"$9